WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:03:08.290
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
03:08.560 --> 03:12.920
I figured out a way to help you get the five million to pay off your debt.

3
03:13.000 --> 03:13.960
PREVIOUSLY

4
03:14.040 --> 03:16.000
Your mom is in gambling debt.

5
03:16.080 --> 03:18.360
You don't have any evidence that Mom stole it.

6
03:18.440 --> 03:21.200
Then check the security cameras.

7
03:21.280 --> 03:23.160
Where are you going, madam?

8
03:23.240 --> 03:24.680
To watch the drama.

9
03:30.320 --> 03:32.600
Chamoi really has to stick her nose into everything.

10
03:32.680 --> 03:34.440
I'll take the bags back for you, honey.

11
03:34.520 --> 03:36.600
-I'll put everything away properly. -Mom, don't.

12
03:48.880 --> 03:49.840
You should go.

13
03:55.400 --> 03:57.240
Where do you want me to go?

14
03:58.000 --> 04:01.040
Anywhere. Go live your own life.

15
04:02.000 --> 04:03.800
Do whatever you want.

16
04:03.880 --> 04:05.320
If you want to gamble, go gamble.

17
04:05.400 --> 04:08.840
If you want a new man, or however many men you want, I won't stop you.

18
04:08.920 --> 04:12.160
It's your life. You get to choose.

19
04:13.160 --> 04:15.880
But they tricked me.

20
04:15.960 --> 04:17.320
I'm telling the truth.

21
04:17.399 --> 04:20.440
Liu was the one who set everything up.

22
04:20.519 --> 04:24.160
You know she's been trying to get us thrown out of this house.

23
04:24.240 --> 04:26.480
And she was the one behind Pong too.

24
04:26.560 --> 04:28.640
I don't care who was behind it.

25
04:29.880 --> 04:33.400
What hurts me is that you broke your promise.

26
04:37.040 --> 04:38.480
You promised me

27
04:38.560 --> 04:40.680
you were going to change

28
04:40.760 --> 04:42.320
and become a better person.

29
04:42.400 --> 04:44.720
You said you wouldn't cause me any more trouble.

30
04:44.800 --> 04:46.440
But you couldn't do it.

31
04:49.400 --> 04:51.680
I made a mistake, sweetheart.

32
04:51.760 --> 04:53.320
I was wrong.

33
04:53.400 --> 04:56.160
Can you forgive me, Hathaya? I'm sorry.

34
04:56.240 --> 04:59.600
How much longer am I supposed to keep listening to your excuses?

35
05:03.160 --> 05:06.000
I promise I'll change.

36
05:06.080 --> 05:09.440
Take me to any temple and make me swear an oath if you want.

37
05:09.520 --> 05:12.360
-Please. -Mom.

38
05:13.000 --> 05:14.800
I want to be happy.

39
05:17.880 --> 05:21.040
Can you give me my life back?

40
05:25.320 --> 05:27.080
Ever since I was born,

41
05:27.920 --> 05:30.400
I've been proud to be your daughter.

42
05:31.080 --> 05:34.120
I've always tried to do the right thing. I've tried to be a good person.

43
05:34.760 --> 05:37.000
But you keep causing problems.

44
05:37.080 --> 05:39.800
And I'm always the one who has to fix them for you.

45
05:47.280 --> 05:49.360
I don't even want to bring up

46
05:51.240 --> 05:53.040
whose actions led to Grandma's death.

47
06:04.360 --> 06:06.000
Forget it, Mom.

48
06:07.600 --> 06:10.360
We can't go back and change the past.

49
06:12.400 --> 06:14.200
I'm only going to look forward now.

50
06:16.720 --> 06:20.280
I want to live my life. I want to be happy.

51
06:20.360 --> 06:23.480
I don't want to spend my life fixing other people's problems anymore.

52
06:27.080 --> 06:29.640
Please give me my life back.

53
06:43.160 --> 06:44.360
Please, Mom.

54
06:51.240 --> 06:52.320
All right.

55
06:54.280 --> 06:55.360
I'll go.

56
06:59.760 --> 07:01.720
But before I leave…

57
07:04.520 --> 07:07.600
can I hug you one last time?

58
07:27.720 --> 07:29.080
Do you know

59
07:30.800 --> 07:33.000
who I love most?

60
07:38.560 --> 07:40.080
Myself.

61
07:41.880 --> 07:43.520
I've only ever thought about myself.

62
07:48.040 --> 07:51.080
But I'm grateful

63
07:52.320 --> 07:54.880
I was born as your grandma's daughter.

64
07:58.800 --> 08:01.120
And the thing I'm proudest of…

65
08:04.240 --> 08:07.000
is that I got to be your mother.

66
08:58.960 --> 09:01.920
Now I understand what you meant when you said

67
09:03.240 --> 09:05.280
some only have parents when it's convenient for them.

68
09:14.840 --> 09:18.360
At least I've succeeded halfway.

69
09:23.720 --> 09:25.080
Everything is spicy.

70
09:25.160 --> 09:27.760
There isn't a single mild dish here. How am I supposed to eat this?

71
09:28.760 --> 09:30.560
-The maid is just-- -Forget it.

72
09:30.640 --> 09:34.000
How many times have I told you there has to be soup or something mild?

73
09:34.080 --> 09:35.840
Why are you so stupid?

74
09:35.920 --> 09:38.240
You never learn.

75
09:47.040 --> 09:48.760
I was trying to tell you

76
09:49.320 --> 09:51.120
that they were bringing the soup and vegetables.

77
09:51.200 --> 09:52.680
Why didn't you say so?

78
09:53.560 --> 09:54.600
You wouldn't listen.

79
09:54.680 --> 09:55.800
Are you talking back to me?

80
09:55.880 --> 09:58.120
Talking back to me?

81
10:00.720 --> 10:02.040
I'm sorry.

82
10:02.120 --> 10:03.320
Remember this.

83
10:04.120 --> 10:08.080
From now on, serve the mild dishes first.

84
10:09.000 --> 10:10.000
Do you understand?

85
10:10.840 --> 10:12.880
Why do I have to teach you something this simple?

86
10:13.480 --> 10:16.160
Even the stupid maids are smarter than you.

87
10:18.120 --> 10:19.440
I'm sorry.

88
10:19.520 --> 10:22.920
You eat first. I'll clean this up.

89
10:23.000 --> 10:25.440
I'm not eating. I'm in no mood for it.

90
10:27.520 --> 10:29.080
I'm going out to eat.

91
10:30.280 --> 10:32.720
So slow. Hurry up.

92
10:32.800 --> 10:33.640
Yeah?

93
10:34.320 --> 10:37.360
You can't do anything right. Stay away from me. You stink.

94
10:38.600 --> 10:39.520
Look.

95
10:40.840 --> 10:42.720
I'm telling you right now.

96
10:42.800 --> 10:45.240
Go upstairs and clean everything up.

97
10:45.320 --> 10:48.200
If I come back and it isn't spotless,

98
10:48.280 --> 10:49.640
you'll regret it.

99
10:51.480 --> 10:52.320
Open it.

100
10:59.400 --> 11:01.920
Give me that. Close it.

101
11:28.720 --> 11:29.680
Ramil.

102
11:29.760 --> 11:32.280
Have you eaten yet? I'll make you something.

103
11:34.080 --> 11:35.400
What happened to your clothes?

104
11:39.040 --> 11:40.480
I was careless earlier.

105
11:40.560 --> 11:44.160
I was bringing the food out and tripped. I spilled it all over myself.

106
11:47.000 --> 11:48.720
If that were really what happened,

107
11:49.400 --> 11:51.920
that man wouldn't have been shouting all over the house.

108
11:52.000 --> 11:53.040
Mom.

109
11:53.760 --> 11:55.440
Stop protecting him.

110
11:55.960 --> 11:59.800
Even though I don't live here anymore, I know what he does to you.

111
12:05.800 --> 12:06.760
Mom.

112
12:07.840 --> 12:09.240
Come live with me.

113
12:10.960 --> 12:14.720
You don't have to stay here as his servant and let him treat you like this. Please.

114
12:17.480 --> 12:18.880
I can't go.

115
12:20.560 --> 12:21.480
Mom.

116
12:22.520 --> 12:24.400
How long are you going to let him hurt you?

117
12:25.320 --> 12:26.680
Do you love him that much?

118
12:28.080 --> 12:29.000
You can't leave him?

119
12:33.840 --> 12:36.240
Mr. Saksit did so much for us.

120
12:37.440 --> 12:40.920
If he hadn't helped us, I don't know what our lives would have been like.

121
12:41.680 --> 12:44.840
Mom, you've repaid him more than enough.

122
12:45.360 --> 12:47.280
How much longer are you going to endure this?

123
12:50.760 --> 12:52.000
I don't know.

124
12:53.640 --> 12:55.000
Maybe my whole life.

125
12:56.480 --> 13:00.160
Or until one of us dies. Maybe then the debt of gratitude will be repaid.

126
13:09.360 --> 13:10.440
I used to think

127
13:11.960 --> 13:13.240
he was the one

128
13:14.000 --> 13:16.080
keeping you chained here.

129
13:17.520 --> 13:18.720
But he isn't.

130
13:19.800 --> 13:21.200
You're the one

131
13:22.440 --> 13:25.640
using that debt of gratitude to imprison yourself.

132
13:29.040 --> 13:29.960
Fine.

133
13:31.240 --> 13:32.520
If you won't come with me,

134
13:35.600 --> 13:36.760
then take care of yourself.

135
13:40.160 --> 13:43.040
Ramil, where are you going?

136
13:51.320 --> 13:52.640
Don't worry about me.

137
13:53.960 --> 13:57.920
Take good care of yourself. Look after your health.

138
13:59.720 --> 14:01.040
I love you, Ramil.

139
14:24.040 --> 14:26.360
Aunt Ann, you can take this out now.

140
14:28.600 --> 14:29.440
Ramil.

141
14:29.520 --> 14:32.120
I'll help carry it.

142
14:34.800 --> 14:38.960
If you came to pick me up, you can wait outside. I can serve it myself.

143
14:41.480 --> 14:43.560
Did you forget? Today's a day off.

144
14:45.680 --> 14:47.600
Then why are you here?

145
14:50.360 --> 14:52.240
You want to know?

146
14:54.360 --> 14:55.960
If you really want to know,

147
14:56.880 --> 14:59.800
bring your ear closer. I'll whisper it to you.

148
15:08.640 --> 15:11.080
I don't want to know anymore.

149
15:11.160 --> 15:15.720
Take this to Grandpa. It's almost time for him to eat and take his medicine.

150
15:15.800 --> 15:16.840
Go.

151
15:16.920 --> 15:19.040
Go on.

152
15:19.120 --> 15:21.600
-You really don't want to know? -Go.

153
15:22.640 --> 15:23.720
Fine.

154
15:32.360 --> 15:33.760
Grandpa.

155
15:33.840 --> 15:37.320
I'm sorry I haven't been around to take care of you much lately.

156
15:38.240 --> 15:40.400
I've been helping Raiwin with his work.

157
15:41.160 --> 15:43.360
He has to thank the villagers,

158
15:43.440 --> 15:46.360
and we've also been discussing some good projects

159
15:46.440 --> 15:47.920
that could support

160
15:48.000 --> 15:51.200
our housing development.

161
15:52.440 --> 15:53.640
That's wonderful, honey.

162
15:53.720 --> 15:56.160
Not only are you a couple,

163
15:56.240 --> 15:59.120
you're supporting each other's businesses too.

164
15:59.200 --> 16:02.960
Grandpa must be so proud of you.

165
16:03.040 --> 16:05.840
Tell Raiwin to resign.

166
16:10.800 --> 16:12.200
Politicians

167
16:12.280 --> 16:16.280
are supposed to work for the community, the people, and the country.

168
16:16.880 --> 16:17.880
They're not supposed

169
16:17.960 --> 16:20.360
to use the office to enrich themselves and help their friends.

170
16:21.720 --> 16:25.560
People like that aren't politicians. They're businessmen.

171
16:26.920 --> 16:28.360
Grandpa.

172
16:29.760 --> 16:33.640
Politicians and business investors need each other.

173
16:34.160 --> 16:35.760
Raiwin became subdistrict chief

174
16:35.840 --> 16:38.080
because I supported him.

175
16:38.600 --> 16:40.200
It's time we got

176
16:40.280 --> 16:43.400
a worthwhile return on our investment.

177
16:43.480 --> 16:45.160
Everyone does it.

178
16:49.040 --> 16:51.040
I'm an old man with a foot in the grave,

179
16:52.080 --> 16:54.320
and Thai politics still hasn't developed at all.

180
16:54.400 --> 16:56.800
It hasn't moved forward.

181
16:57.720 --> 17:00.120
People say Thai dramas are trash.

182
17:00.720 --> 17:02.040
But I don't think so.

183
17:02.880 --> 17:05.359
Thai politics is far worse.

184
17:14.319 --> 17:15.760
Why did the food take so long?

185
17:15.839 --> 17:18.960
Were you waiting for us to beg for our lives?

186
17:19.960 --> 17:23.800
I'm not late. You came early.

187
17:23.880 --> 17:24.880
You're just hangry.

188
17:28.680 --> 17:30.400
The food is here.

189
17:30.480 --> 17:32.240
This is yours, sir.

190
17:33.000 --> 17:36.640
Is this even your job?

191
17:37.160 --> 17:39.280
You're done now. Go.

192
17:51.840 --> 17:53.160
What are you staring at?

193
17:53.240 --> 17:55.200
Eat. It'll get cold.

194
17:57.400 --> 18:00.560
Ramil, this isn't your place.

195
18:02.720 --> 18:04.080
Didn't you hear what Mom said?

196
18:04.760 --> 18:05.960
Hathaya.

197
18:07.000 --> 18:10.640
You should teach your husband some manners.

198
18:13.520 --> 18:14.560
Ramil.

199
18:15.480 --> 18:17.200
Go wait for me--

200
18:17.280 --> 18:19.200
I invited Ramil to eat with us.

201
18:26.000 --> 18:30.640
Father, I know you're pleased with Ramil's work,

202
18:31.360 --> 18:33.440
but I really don't think this is appropriate.

203
18:34.160 --> 18:37.720
I don't eat at the same table as workers.

204
18:41.680 --> 18:44.160
If it makes you uncomfortable,

205
18:44.240 --> 18:46.760
you and your daughter can eat separately in the kitchen.

206
18:53.120 --> 18:54.160
Hathaya.

207
18:54.840 --> 18:57.200
After you finish eating, prepare a room for Ramil.

208
19:00.720 --> 19:03.080
What room, Grandpa?

209
19:04.680 --> 19:06.840
Ramil is your husband.

210
19:07.360 --> 19:08.840
It's time he moved in with you.

211
19:15.640 --> 19:16.480
Father.

212
19:17.080 --> 19:20.440
Father, you're going to let Ramil live here?

213
19:20.520 --> 19:21.600
You can't.

214
19:21.680 --> 19:25.280
This man has a bad history. He once tried to violate Hathaya in her room.

215
19:25.360 --> 19:27.560
What if one day he loses control

216
19:27.640 --> 19:29.960
and goes after Chayanee too?

217
19:32.000 --> 19:34.280
From what I know of Ramil,

218
19:34.920 --> 19:36.280
he isn't that kind of man.

219
19:39.560 --> 19:42.120
But if it makes you uncomfortable,

220
19:42.920 --> 19:43.760
I won't push it.

221
19:47.960 --> 19:51.000
You and your daughter can move out and live somewhere else.

222
19:54.480 --> 19:58.000
If your things are too heavy, I can help carry them.

223
20:02.760 --> 20:04.120
No.

224
20:05.040 --> 20:06.400
I'm staying here.

225
20:07.280 --> 20:08.360
This is my house.

226
20:14.720 --> 20:15.880
For you.

227
20:34.360 --> 20:36.000
Why do you have to live here?

228
20:36.080 --> 20:39.440
Grandpa said we're husband and wife.

229
20:39.520 --> 20:40.640
We have to be together.

230
20:43.000 --> 20:46.680
I don't believe that. I know you were the one who asked Grandpa.

231
20:49.400 --> 20:51.920
You know a lot, huh?

232
20:52.600 --> 20:54.880
Chayanee and Liu

233
20:54.960 --> 20:57.200
keep attacking you and trying to get rid of you.

234
20:57.720 --> 20:58.760
Look.

235
20:59.400 --> 21:00.880
I'm worried about you.

236
21:01.840 --> 21:03.040
So I'm looking after you.

237
21:19.960 --> 21:21.040
This looks comfortable.

238
21:22.520 --> 21:24.480
You can't. Get up.

239
21:24.560 --> 21:26.520
-Why? -We can't sleep together. Get up.

240
21:26.600 --> 21:28.000
I don't want us sleeping together.

241
21:28.080 --> 21:30.520
-We can sleep together. Why not? -No, we can't.

242
21:30.600 --> 21:32.440
-No. -I don't mind.

243
21:32.520 --> 21:34.120
I do.

244
22:01.280 --> 22:03.880
You can sleep on the bed.

245
22:03.960 --> 22:06.680
I'll put a mattress on the floor.

246
22:07.280 --> 22:08.800
Come on.

247
22:08.880 --> 22:11.800
Everyone knows we're husband and wife.

248
22:11.880 --> 22:14.440
We can sleep together. I don't mind. Come here.

249
22:16.000 --> 22:18.240
Do you remember what you once told me?

250
22:22.080 --> 22:24.360
You said you could never love someone like me.

251
22:25.840 --> 22:29.440
But thank you for coming here

252
22:29.520 --> 22:32.400
to look after me as a coworker.

253
22:36.320 --> 22:38.520
I'm going to get some things for you.

254
22:39.080 --> 22:39.920
Wait--

255
22:43.200 --> 22:46.800
Damn it. Why did I ever say that?

256
22:55.280 --> 22:57.760
Raiwin, is your father home?

257
22:57.840 --> 22:59.800
I need to talk to him.

258
22:59.880 --> 23:01.920
You should go home now.

259
23:02.000 --> 23:03.120
Please.

260
23:04.240 --> 23:07.720
Why? I'm here to talk about our wedding.

261
23:09.280 --> 23:10.760
Today probably isn't a good time.

262
23:11.280 --> 23:13.240
Go home. I'll call you later.

263
23:14.360 --> 23:15.760
But we already agreed

264
23:15.840 --> 23:18.720
that after the election, we would get married.

265
23:19.400 --> 23:21.040
Is your father going back on his word?

266
23:22.960 --> 23:24.000
It's not like that.

267
23:24.080 --> 23:27.600
Then I'm talking to him today.

268
23:28.880 --> 23:29.960
Chayanee.

269
23:31.120 --> 23:33.280
They're deliberately framing me.

270
23:35.200 --> 23:36.520
They're trying to discredit me.

271
23:36.600 --> 23:39.240
Damn it! What the hell is this?

272
23:41.160 --> 23:42.720
Here's the coffee you asked for.

273
23:42.800 --> 23:44.280
I don't want it.

274
23:45.360 --> 23:47.280
I told you I'm in a bad mood.

275
23:48.560 --> 23:49.640
Geez.

276
23:53.320 --> 23:55.160
They're trying to discredit me.

277
23:56.040 --> 23:57.000
Dad.

278
23:57.880 --> 24:01.200
I already told you I'm not seeing anyone.

279
24:01.280 --> 24:02.520
Get them out of here.

280
24:03.480 --> 24:05.600
You can't throw me out, Uncle.

281
24:06.280 --> 24:08.360
I have something important to discuss with you.

282
24:11.360 --> 24:12.720
I'm sorry.

283
24:13.440 --> 24:15.800
Can we talk another day? Today really isn't convenient.

284
24:15.880 --> 24:18.560
But today is convenient for me. And I want to talk now.

285
24:22.920 --> 24:25.480
Please listen to me. Go home now.

286
24:26.000 --> 24:28.240
How about we go get something to eat? Come on.

287
24:28.320 --> 24:32.240
No. I don't want to spend time with you today.

288
24:32.320 --> 24:35.000
I want to settle this with your father.

289
24:35.080 --> 24:37.360
Then say whatever you came to say and get it over with.

290
24:37.440 --> 24:40.600
I spent money helping Raiwin win the election.

291
24:40.680 --> 24:43.680
You promised me that if Raiwin became subdistrict chief,

292
24:43.760 --> 24:45.600
you'd ask Grandpa for my hand in marriage.

293
24:45.680 --> 24:47.480
And it's been a long time already.

294
24:47.560 --> 24:50.200
I've been busy. It hasn't been convenient.

295
24:50.280 --> 24:51.320
Can we do it later?

296
24:51.400 --> 24:52.720
I want to talk about it today.

297
24:52.800 --> 24:54.120
What is your problem?

298
24:54.200 --> 24:56.160
I've waited long enough.

299
24:56.240 --> 24:59.440
And your son can't be trusted. He keeps going after Hathaya.

300
24:59.520 --> 25:01.480
That's why I hired those men to rape her.

301
25:01.560 --> 25:03.600
It's just a shame they failed.

302
25:03.680 --> 25:05.880
You hired men to rape Hathaya?

303
25:07.880 --> 25:10.600
How could you do that? She's your relative.

304
25:10.680 --> 25:12.640
I've never considered her family.

305
25:12.720 --> 25:15.240
Do you even realize what you've done?

306
25:15.320 --> 25:18.520
Don't defend her. And don't try to change the subject.

307
25:18.600 --> 25:21.360
Today, you are going to ask Grandpa for my hand.

308
25:22.360 --> 25:24.280
I'm under investigation for old cases.

309
25:24.360 --> 25:27.680
The streetlight case. The landfill case. God knows what else.

310
25:27.760 --> 25:29.160
I could go to prison.

311
25:29.800 --> 25:33.080
How am I supposed to be in the mood to arrange your wedding?

312
25:39.480 --> 25:40.520
Uncle.

313
25:41.120 --> 25:45.240
Will shouting like this keep you out of prison?

314
25:49.920 --> 25:52.160
Cases like this take money.

315
25:53.080 --> 25:56.280
If you need money, ask Grandpa.

316
25:56.360 --> 25:57.680
I'll help talk to him.

317
25:59.040 --> 26:00.600
Why…

318
26:01.760 --> 26:03.960
Why would your grandfather help me?

319
26:04.640 --> 26:07.200
If Raiwin and I get married,

320
26:07.280 --> 26:09.680
our two families will become one.

321
26:10.440 --> 26:13.320
Grandpa will have to help his own family.

322
26:15.040 --> 26:17.640
And the sooner I get married,

323
26:17.720 --> 26:20.160
the sooner I'll have a chance of receiving

324
26:20.240 --> 26:21.720
Grandpa's inheritance.

325
26:26.200 --> 26:27.240
Raiwin.

326
26:28.960 --> 26:31.280
We're going to Mr. Pichai's house.

327
26:32.320 --> 26:33.200
Alright.

328
27:06.000 --> 27:07.520
Well, former subdistrict chief.

329
27:08.040 --> 27:10.400
I'll skip the formal greeting.

330
27:10.480 --> 27:11.880
You don't like me anyway,

331
27:11.960 --> 27:15.120
and I don't respect you.

332
27:15.200 --> 27:16.160
Really?

333
27:16.680 --> 27:19.760
Whether you greet me properly or not, I don't care.

334
27:20.960 --> 27:23.120
Ever since you left my house,

335
27:24.920 --> 27:28.160
you've become a parasite living off a woman here?

336
27:31.320 --> 27:33.120
Living off a woman now, are you?

337
27:35.040 --> 27:36.200
Ramil.

338
27:36.280 --> 27:38.160
I live here because

339
27:38.920 --> 27:42.760
Mr. Pichai asked me to help with the work and to screen anyone coming in

340
27:43.400 --> 27:45.800
so nothing inauspicious gets into the house.

341
27:46.400 --> 27:47.480
-That's too much-- -Dad.

342
27:51.480 --> 27:53.640
Dad and I have business with Mr. Pichai.

343
27:54.960 --> 27:56.680
I already told Grandpa we were coming.

344
27:57.320 --> 27:59.440
As for you,

345
27:59.520 --> 28:01.200
go back to the workers' quarters.

346
28:02.560 --> 28:03.720
Hathaya.

347
28:03.800 --> 28:07.560
Take your worker husband back to your area.

348
28:07.640 --> 28:09.560
Don't let him bark at the guests.

349
28:10.200 --> 28:13.280
And if you can't train him and he keeps barking,

350
28:13.360 --> 28:15.680
get a muzzle

351
28:15.760 --> 28:17.440
and chain him up.

352
28:21.000 --> 28:22.480
We told you to leave, so go.

353
28:24.040 --> 28:26.840
Both of you. I can't stand looking at your faces.

354
28:27.480 --> 28:29.760
If you made an appointment with Grandpa,

355
28:29.840 --> 28:32.120
you'll have to put up with looking at our faces.

356
28:32.200 --> 28:34.080
Grandpa told Ramil and me to take care of you.

357
28:40.280 --> 28:43.680
Well? What do you say, former subdistrict chief? What should we do?

358
28:49.680 --> 28:50.800
Ramil.

359
28:51.840 --> 28:55.320
Please let Mr. Pichai know my father has arrived.

360
28:57.440 --> 28:59.280
Since becoming subdistrict chief,

361
28:59.800 --> 29:01.280
you've become much more polite.

362
29:02.960 --> 29:03.800
Fine.

363
29:04.400 --> 29:05.280
Come on.

364
29:11.400 --> 29:13.840
Please be patient, Mr. Saksit.

365
29:13.920 --> 29:17.440
It won't be long before Chayanee marries Raiwin.

366
29:17.520 --> 29:21.000
Once that happens, we'll throw him out.

367
29:23.480 --> 29:26.960
Please come in. Father is waiting.

368
29:27.040 --> 29:28.160
-Thank you. -Wow.

369
29:28.680 --> 29:30.880
What beautiful flowers.

370
29:33.120 --> 29:34.760
Father is waiting.

371
29:35.320 --> 29:36.560
Come on.

372
29:37.920 --> 29:39.000
Please.

373
29:39.080 --> 29:40.440
-Hello, Mr. Pichai. -Hello.

374
29:40.520 --> 29:41.360
Here.

375
29:41.440 --> 29:42.720
For you, sir.

376
29:43.560 --> 29:44.440
-Thank you. -Hello.

377
29:46.360 --> 29:48.480
Mr. Saksit.

378
29:48.560 --> 29:51.880
You can get to the point. I don't have much time.

379
29:51.960 --> 29:54.240
It'll soon be time for me to eat and take my medicine.

380
29:55.120 --> 29:56.400
I've come to formally

381
29:56.480 --> 29:59.360
ask for Chayanee's hand in marriage

382
29:59.440 --> 30:01.120
for my son Raiwin.

383
30:06.440 --> 30:09.000
What do you think, Father? I have no objection.

384
30:09.080 --> 30:13.080
Raiwin is a good man. He has a good career

385
30:13.160 --> 30:15.800
and comes from a good family.

386
30:17.800 --> 30:22.000
A person's career and family status are only secondary.

387
30:22.080 --> 30:23.880
What matters most

388
30:25.640 --> 30:27.840
is character and whether two people can live together.

389
30:30.160 --> 30:32.320
What do you think of Raiwin?

390
30:37.880 --> 30:40.120
Raiwin has never

391
30:40.200 --> 30:42.280
disappointed me or made me sad.

392
30:42.800 --> 30:47.680
Whenever I'm with him, I feel safe.

393
30:47.760 --> 30:51.080
We complete each other, Grandpa.

394
30:53.760 --> 30:56.720
If you've made up your mind, I won't object.

395
30:56.800 --> 30:58.600
Okay.

396
30:58.680 --> 31:00.400
Thank you very much, Mr. Pichai.

397
31:00.480 --> 31:01.600
I'll start

398
31:01.680 --> 31:04.920
preparing the wedding and find an auspicious date as soon as possible.

399
31:06.200 --> 31:08.480
If that's everything, I'm going to rest.

400
31:12.920 --> 31:13.760
Grandpa.

401
31:14.640 --> 31:16.680
Mr. Saksit served

402
31:16.760 --> 31:21.680
as subdistrict chief honestly and sincerely for our community.

403
31:25.880 --> 31:28.040
You said this concerns Mr. Saksit,

404
31:28.120 --> 31:31.480
so he should be the one to speak.

405
31:36.720 --> 31:38.840
Well, Mr. Pichai,

406
31:39.360 --> 31:42.280
I'm being politically persecuted.

407
31:42.360 --> 31:45.360
The people who lost to Raiwin

408
31:45.440 --> 31:47.480
filed complaints accusing me

409
31:47.560 --> 31:50.640
of corruption involving various Subdistrict Office projects.

410
31:51.400 --> 31:54.560
So I was hoping you could support me

411
31:57.400 --> 31:58.640
with around

412
31:59.720 --> 32:02.920
ten million baht. I could use the money to take care of the cases.

413
32:03.760 --> 32:04.640
Well…

414
32:05.560 --> 32:07.760
But I promise you, Mr. Pichai,

415
32:08.480 --> 32:13.160
the return you'll receive will be worth far more than ten million.

416
32:13.680 --> 32:15.760
I'll have Raiwin

417
32:15.840 --> 32:18.520
approve a new road project

418
32:18.600 --> 32:21.400
that runs through your land.

419
32:28.680 --> 32:30.760
A road through my land?

420
32:32.640 --> 32:36.360
That could increase its value tenfold or twentyfold.

421
32:38.440 --> 32:40.320
Thank you very much.

422
32:41.320 --> 32:42.760
Thank you, Mr. Pichai,

423
32:42.840 --> 32:45.120
for supporting me.

424
32:45.200 --> 32:48.360
But I still have three questions.

425
32:50.200 --> 32:51.480
First.

426
32:53.040 --> 32:55.520
Can money really make a corruption case go away?

427
33:01.480 --> 33:02.600
Mr. Pichai.

428
33:03.680 --> 33:07.400
Money can settle cases. I've done it before.

429
33:08.000 --> 33:12.280
Second. If the road goes through my land,

430
33:13.560 --> 33:15.000
what do the people get out of it?

431
33:17.080 --> 33:19.640
If the road goes through your land,

432
33:20.160 --> 33:21.440
the locals don't get anything.

433
33:21.520 --> 33:23.440
You do.

434
33:23.520 --> 33:26.480
But I already had Raiwin prepare other projects.

435
33:26.560 --> 33:28.960
An anti-drug sports initiative.

436
33:29.040 --> 33:32.800
Distributing goods to poor families.

437
33:32.880 --> 33:36.680
Projects like that will definitely benefit the villagers.

438
33:37.960 --> 33:39.000
Third.

439
33:41.760 --> 33:43.600
Is Raiwin chief, or are you still in charge?

440
33:45.680 --> 33:46.840
Of course Raiwin is.

441
33:47.440 --> 33:49.400
Young people

442
33:49.480 --> 33:51.520
are popular these days,

443
33:51.600 --> 33:53.840
so Raiwin

444
33:53.920 --> 33:57.000
has to be the face, but I still

445
33:57.080 --> 33:58.760
handle the administration.

446
34:00.880 --> 34:03.680
Then Raiwin is just your puppet?

447
34:08.719 --> 34:11.440
From all three of your answers,

448
34:11.520 --> 34:14.120
I still don't see anything you're doing for the people.

449
34:14.639 --> 34:16.000
All I see is what benefits you

450
34:18.400 --> 34:19.480
and your friends.

451
34:22.560 --> 34:25.400
And one more thing. I don't support passing power down like this.

452
34:27.440 --> 34:31.120
The era of old dinosaurs like you is over.

453
34:34.880 --> 34:36.400
What exactly do you want?

454
34:38.880 --> 34:41.239
I wasted my time coming here just to be insulted.

455
34:41.320 --> 34:43.520
Are you going to help me or not?

456
34:49.920 --> 34:51.600
I'm one of the locals.

457
34:52.239 --> 34:55.440
I want politicians who work for people like me.

458
34:58.680 --> 35:01.760
If you're not ready to be good politicians,

459
35:01.840 --> 35:03.040
then resign.

460
35:03.840 --> 35:05.920
Don't become political parasites.

461
35:11.480 --> 35:13.280
Ramil. Take me to rest.

462
35:13.360 --> 35:14.440
-Yes, sir. -Raiwin.

463
35:15.160 --> 35:16.000
We're leaving.

464
35:21.520 --> 35:22.680
Chayanee.

465
35:24.680 --> 35:27.000
Uncle. Uncle.

466
35:31.840 --> 35:33.000
Uncle.

467
35:33.880 --> 35:37.000
Uncle. Please calm down.

468
35:37.640 --> 35:38.840
Calm down?

469
35:40.160 --> 35:42.600
I'm facing criminal charges and you want me to calm down?

470
35:43.240 --> 35:44.920
You said if we discussed the wedding,

471
35:45.000 --> 35:46.800
your grandfather

472
35:47.320 --> 35:50.040
would treat me like family and help me.

473
35:50.120 --> 35:52.600
And what happened? What was that?

474
35:53.200 --> 35:55.400
Your grandfather

475
35:55.480 --> 35:59.040
tore me apart. What the hell was that?

476
36:00.920 --> 36:02.000
Grandpa is--

477
36:02.520 --> 36:05.080
He's old-fashioned. He clings to all those ridiculous ideals.

478
36:05.160 --> 36:06.560
I'll

479
36:06.640 --> 36:10.400
talk to him again and try to persuade him.

480
36:10.920 --> 36:13.280
Grandpa has probably been manipulated

481
36:13.360 --> 36:14.360
by Ramil and Hathaya.

482
36:15.040 --> 36:16.640
For now, Mr. Saksit,

483
36:16.720 --> 36:20.120
start preparing the dowry. Chayanee and I

484
36:20.200 --> 36:22.520
will find a way to help you.

485
36:22.600 --> 36:23.600
Okay?

486
36:28.640 --> 36:30.160
If Mr. Pichai

487
36:31.000 --> 36:32.360
won't help me,

488
36:35.320 --> 36:37.080
then forget joining our families.

489
36:40.000 --> 36:42.440
There will be no wedding.

490
36:43.680 --> 36:47.120
No. My daughter's reputation will be ruined.

491
36:47.200 --> 36:48.200
Oh my God.

492
36:48.960 --> 36:49.800
Raiwin.

493
36:50.960 --> 36:54.120
You can't abandon me. I've helped you so much.

494
36:57.280 --> 36:58.960
You know I can't do anything about this.

495
36:59.600 --> 37:01.760
My father decides everything.

496
37:03.080 --> 37:04.160
We'll talk later.

497
37:05.600 --> 37:07.640
No. There has to be a wedding.

498
37:08.240 --> 37:11.720
Chayanee, calm down. Lower your voice.

499
37:11.800 --> 37:15.040
I won't accept this, Mom. Raiwin can't leave me.

500
37:15.120 --> 37:16.480
Calm down, sweetheart.

501
37:16.560 --> 37:18.080
Dad.

502
37:18.160 --> 37:22.000
I'll try talking to Chayanee and ask for another meeting with Mr. Pichai.

503
37:22.600 --> 37:23.840
Don't.

504
37:23.920 --> 37:26.600
I'll put together a concrete proposal

505
37:27.120 --> 37:29.840
and write out the benefits Mr. Pichai would receive.

506
37:30.600 --> 37:32.400
I think he might change his mind.

507
37:32.480 --> 37:35.240
I told you not to bother.

508
37:35.320 --> 37:39.240
That Pichai is dumber than the ancient dinosaurs he keeps rambling about.

509
37:39.320 --> 37:42.000
He clings to all these idiotic ideals.

510
37:42.080 --> 37:46.680
I offered him a project that could make him a billionaire.

511
37:46.760 --> 37:49.160
Stuff money in his coffin, he still won't care.

512
37:49.240 --> 37:51.520
I'm trying to help you.

513
37:52.200 --> 37:53.520
What do you want me to do?

514
37:54.120 --> 37:55.240
What do I want you to do?

515
37:56.560 --> 37:57.480
You.

516
37:58.000 --> 37:59.120
Break up with Chayanee.

517
38:00.720 --> 38:02.040
She probably won't accept that.

518
38:05.200 --> 38:06.280
You're a man.

519
38:11.480 --> 38:14.080
Don't let a woman lead you around by the nose!

520
38:14.160 --> 38:16.280
You're a man, not a buffalo.

521
38:16.800 --> 38:19.520
I've never let a woman push me around.

522
38:19.600 --> 38:21.320
We control them.

523
38:23.000 --> 38:24.440
If Chayanee can't help us anymore,

524
38:24.520 --> 38:25.920
then break up with her.

525
38:26.000 --> 38:30.320
I'll find you a woman who's better and more capable myself.

526
38:31.880 --> 38:34.640
Can't you let me think and handle my own life for once?

527
38:36.760 --> 38:37.600
Think?

528
38:38.120 --> 38:40.240
You're too stupid to think for yourself.

529
38:41.040 --> 38:44.680
Why is Ramil doing so well now? Because of Pichai.

530
38:44.760 --> 38:47.160
Pichai loves him and trusts him.

531
38:47.240 --> 38:50.840
If that old man dies and Hathaya inherits everything,

532
38:50.920 --> 38:52.440
do you understand what that means?

533
38:52.520 --> 38:54.440
Ramil will end up even better off than you.

534
38:54.520 --> 38:57.080
And worst of all, he'll stand over your head.

535
38:57.160 --> 38:59.320
He'll spit down on you.

536
38:59.920 --> 39:01.000
Do you know

537
39:02.040 --> 39:03.360
why that old Pichai

538
39:03.440 --> 39:05.600
refused to help me? Because of Ramil.

539
39:05.680 --> 39:08.160
He keeps turning Pichai against us.

540
39:08.240 --> 39:10.120
Damn it. Idiot.

541
39:14.720 --> 39:16.920
Go. Why are you still standing there?

542
39:17.000 --> 39:18.200
‎Go.

543
39:21.400 --> 39:23.040
Nothing ever goes the way I want.

544
39:31.960 --> 39:33.280
Did you get what I asked for?

545
39:39.080 --> 39:41.520
Why is there so little? There should be more than this.

546
39:43.000 --> 39:44.640
This is really all I have left.

547
39:44.720 --> 39:46.960
How can this be all that's left?

548
39:47.040 --> 39:49.800
I bought you jewelry to wear to events.

549
39:50.480 --> 39:53.240
You already made me sell it when you were campaigning.

550
39:53.320 --> 39:54.880
You spent all that money.

551
39:56.080 --> 39:58.200
What the hell?

552
39:58.960 --> 40:01.600
Do you understand how much money I need to settle these cases?

553
40:01.680 --> 40:03.880
Get it?

554
40:09.160 --> 40:10.960
The ring. Take it off.

555
40:17.040 --> 40:18.280
That's Anon's, right?

556
40:19.480 --> 40:21.120
You love him that much?

557
40:21.720 --> 40:23.000
You won't take it off?

558
40:23.080 --> 40:25.560
It's my wedding ring. I want to keep it for Ramil.

559
40:25.640 --> 40:27.000
No. Take it off.

560
40:27.080 --> 40:29.520
-No. -Take it off.

561
40:29.600 --> 40:31.120
-It's the only thing I-- -Give me.

562
40:31.200 --> 40:33.840
-Give it to me. -Please let me keep it.

563
40:33.920 --> 40:35.000
No.

564
40:35.080 --> 40:37.360
Don't take it. I want to save it for Ramil.

565
40:37.440 --> 40:39.360
Do you? I won't let you.

566
40:39.440 --> 40:40.280
Give it here.

567
40:42.680 --> 40:44.520
Please let me keep it.

568
40:44.600 --> 40:46.520
Nothing belongs to you.

569
40:46.600 --> 40:48.120
Not even you.

570
40:48.640 --> 40:51.600
You belong to me. Remember that.

571
40:53.040 --> 40:55.880
No. Don't take it. Please.

572
40:55.960 --> 40:57.960
You're begging?

573
40:58.040 --> 40:59.560
Please.

574
41:01.280 --> 41:03.800
Mr. Saksit, have you ever loved me at all?

575
41:14.840 --> 41:15.800
I brought your money.

576
41:26.160 --> 41:27.000
Paying me back?

577
41:30.000 --> 41:31.280
How much do you want this time?

578
41:34.160 --> 41:35.600
I'm only here to repay you.

579
41:38.200 --> 41:40.480
I invested that money with a friend.

580
41:40.560 --> 41:42.320
Things are going well now.

581
41:43.920 --> 41:45.280
I wish I could repay you more,

582
41:46.440 --> 41:48.360
but we're only just getting started.

583
41:49.200 --> 41:51.160
I'm sorry it took me so long.

584
41:54.840 --> 41:56.360
I won't take up any more of your time.

585
41:58.000 --> 41:59.800
I know you don't want to see me.

586
42:03.840 --> 42:05.000
I'll go.

587
42:20.920 --> 42:22.760
Your father kept his word.

588
42:23.280 --> 42:25.320
Can you forgive him now?

589
42:33.800 --> 42:35.800
Even if he pays back a thousand times more,

590
42:39.120 --> 42:40.720
money can't buy our happiness back.

591
42:49.720 --> 42:51.360
Whose car is that?

592
42:51.440 --> 42:53.120
Ms. Sanguansri has a visitor.

593
42:54.040 --> 42:56.280
-Who? -Mr. Anon.

594
43:05.680 --> 43:06.880
What do you need?

595
43:06.960 --> 43:10.080
You could've called to meet somewhere. I don't want you here.

596
43:11.560 --> 43:13.920
I needed to see you about something important.

597
43:14.600 --> 43:16.960
The business I started with my friend is doing well.

598
43:18.440 --> 43:21.880
I'm happy for you. But if that's all, you should go.

599
43:24.160 --> 43:25.680
I understand.

600
43:26.680 --> 43:29.200
If Mr. Saksit sees me here, he won't be happy.

601
43:35.680 --> 43:36.640
Here.

602
43:37.360 --> 43:38.560
I brought the money back.

603
43:38.640 --> 43:39.960
TEN MILLION

604
43:42.760 --> 43:44.880
I'm trying to make everything better.

605
43:46.880 --> 43:48.840
I want you and our son to have a good life.

606
43:52.600 --> 43:54.920
And I've always felt guilty

607
43:55.720 --> 43:57.520
and ashamed

608
43:58.600 --> 44:00.400
for abandoning you both.

609
44:05.080 --> 44:08.080
Thank you so much for returning the money.

610
44:08.840 --> 44:12.320
Ramil intended to use it to build a house.

611
44:13.120 --> 44:15.680
He's always dreamed of having a home of his own.

612
44:21.920 --> 44:24.080
I may never get the chance to be a good husband.

613
44:26.080 --> 44:28.520
But I want to be a good father to our son.

614
44:30.840 --> 44:32.880
And I'll bring more money for you and Ramil.

615
44:39.960 --> 44:41.160
Sanguansri.

616
44:42.520 --> 44:43.880
What happened to your face?

617
44:48.240 --> 44:50.360
Nothing. I fell.

618
44:50.880 --> 44:52.160
If that's all, please go.

619
45:07.840 --> 45:09.440
Thank you for taking the time

620
45:09.520 --> 45:11.760
to have coffee with me, Ingorn.

621
45:13.000 --> 45:15.160
I should be thanking you, Chief.

622
45:15.240 --> 45:18.120
I know how busy you are.

623
45:19.440 --> 45:22.440
No matter how busy I am, I can always make time for you.

624
45:24.680 --> 45:25.920
Today,

625
45:26.000 --> 45:29.800
I also have a good project to present to you.

626
45:33.440 --> 45:35.440
If I build a road through here,

627
45:35.520 --> 45:37.080
the value of this land

628
45:37.600 --> 45:39.680
will increase several times over.

629
45:41.120 --> 45:43.000
I'll also make sure

630
45:43.080 --> 45:45.960
the electricity and water systems are fully developed.

631
45:47.160 --> 45:48.800
What do you think?

632
45:49.840 --> 45:52.440
Chief, you're being so good to me.

633
45:53.520 --> 45:55.320
How am I supposed to repay you?

634
45:59.880 --> 46:01.200
You don't need to repay me.

635
46:04.160 --> 46:07.160
As long as we cooperate, everything will work out.

636
46:15.640 --> 46:17.560
If you keep treating me like this,

637
46:18.080 --> 46:20.560
won't your girlfriend tear me apart?

638
46:22.360 --> 46:23.360
No, she won't.

639
46:29.480 --> 46:31.720
-Your drinks. -I'll serve it.

640
46:34.920 --> 46:37.320
Hey. What are you doing?

641
46:38.800 --> 46:42.200
I'm the one who should be asking what you're doing.

642
46:42.800 --> 46:45.920
I'm discussing business with Raiwin. What does that have to do with you?

643
46:46.520 --> 46:49.920
What's that got to do with me? You can say that with a straight face?

644
46:50.440 --> 46:53.960
Raiwin is my boyfriend. Everyone in the restaurant knows he's my boyfriend.

645
46:56.280 --> 46:59.000
Raiwin, I'm leaving.

646
47:00.360 --> 47:01.560
Come on. I'll take you.

647
47:04.200 --> 47:05.200
Chayanee.

648
47:05.280 --> 47:08.680
Thanks for remembering my name.

649
47:08.760 --> 47:12.000
Now burn this into your skull too.

650
47:12.080 --> 47:13.440
Raiwin is mine.

651
47:13.520 --> 47:16.080
Stay away from my man.

652
47:16.160 --> 47:17.680
That's enough.

653
47:18.200 --> 47:20.640
I'm reporting you to the police. I'll press charges.

654
47:20.720 --> 47:22.840
Go ahead. I can afford it.

655
47:24.040 --> 47:25.480
Charge me by the slap.

656
47:28.120 --> 47:29.720
You think you're the only one with money?

657
47:29.800 --> 47:32.920
You slapped me? You just declared war on me.

658
47:37.200 --> 47:38.320
Enough.

659
47:38.400 --> 47:40.000
Both of you.

660
47:40.080 --> 47:41.000
Stop.

661
47:41.520 --> 47:42.480
Raiwin.

662
47:42.560 --> 47:43.800
Enough.

663
47:45.160 --> 47:47.200
Come on. I'll walk you out.

664
47:52.240 --> 47:53.600
You damaged the restaurant.

665
47:53.680 --> 47:55.160
You have to pay for it,

666
47:55.240 --> 47:57.360
or I'll call the police.

667
48:02.520 --> 48:05.200
Even if I destroyed the entire restaurant, I could afford it.

668
48:05.720 --> 48:07.360
Remember that. I'm rich.

669
48:09.120 --> 48:11.160
I'm really sorry, Ingorn.

670
48:11.680 --> 48:13.080
Go take care of your girlfriend.

671
48:13.160 --> 48:16.480
Ingorn, I'm really sorry.

672
48:17.520 --> 48:20.000
There's nothing between Chayanee and me anymore.

673
48:20.080 --> 48:21.560
I apologize again.

674
48:23.320 --> 48:25.680
And please keep my project in mind.

675
48:26.440 --> 48:27.480
Please.

676
48:30.200 --> 48:32.160
You shameless bitch. You're educated.

677
48:32.240 --> 48:35.080
Can't you find your own husband? Do you have to steal someone else's?

678
48:35.600 --> 48:38.640
Come back and slap me again. Then you'll know I fight back.

679
48:38.720 --> 48:39.560
Come back.

680
48:39.640 --> 48:41.800
Enough.

681
48:46.120 --> 48:49.120
Instead of taking my side, you're protecting her.

682
48:49.200 --> 48:50.240
Stop acting crazy.

683
48:50.320 --> 48:51.720
I'm crazy because of you.

684
48:51.800 --> 48:54.280
I warned you. If you break up with me,

685
48:54.360 --> 48:55.280
you're going to regret it.

686
48:55.360 --> 48:56.600
What the hell do you expect?

687
48:56.680 --> 48:58.040
You promised

688
48:58.120 --> 49:00.160
Grandpa would help my father.

689
49:00.920 --> 49:02.440
You couldn't make it happen.

690
49:03.840 --> 49:05.720
My father is pressuring me too.

691
49:06.480 --> 49:08.240
You can do whatever you want,

692
49:08.320 --> 49:10.000
but you are not getting another woman.

693
49:14.440 --> 49:16.680
If you don't want me seeing someone else,

694
49:18.920 --> 49:20.320
then find the money for me.

695
49:27.040 --> 49:29.440
What do you mean by that?

696
49:30.160 --> 49:33.400
If I can't find the money to help your father settle his case,

697
49:33.920 --> 49:35.680
you're going to find another woman?

698
49:37.000 --> 49:37.840
Answer me.

699
49:55.200 --> 49:56.720
Raiwin threatened to break up with me.

700
49:56.800 --> 49:58.760
Where else am I supposed to find the money?

701
49:58.840 --> 50:00.240
I came to give you the money.

702
50:00.320 --> 50:02.960
And I had no idea Pong was going to show up.

703
50:03.040 --> 50:06.320
If Grandpa dies, his inheritance

704
50:06.400 --> 50:08.680
will go to you.

705
50:08.760 --> 50:11.280
If Grandpa won't give it to me, then I won't ask.

706
50:11.360 --> 50:12.640
I'll steal it.

707
50:12.720 --> 50:14.440
All this time, I let you take care of Grandpa.

708
50:14.520 --> 50:16.680
But you almost got him killed.

709
52:11.040 --> 52:12.960
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
